                <pb facs="0016" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845C.00/9–2846: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Rangoon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Packer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rangoon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-28">September 28, 1946</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        28—12:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>317. May 316, 27th.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d4-f1"/> In broadcast evening 26th when
                    he announced new Executive Council Governor noted three main causes of
                    dissatisfaction with present state of affairs in Burma: (1) Doubts about powers
                    of Executive Council, (2) Burmans not “associated with” defense and external
                    affairs, (3) criticism of HMG’s financial
                    control. Also Executive Council not in touch with frontier areas policy.</p>
                <p>Governor proposed following solutions: (1) “It is my firm intention to see” that
                    Executive Council has same authority Ministers had under 1935 act, (2) Burman
                    Counsellor for Defense and External Affairs who will also be member of Executive
                    Council without portfolio and Deputy Chairman. This is position given Aung San,
                    (3) HMG agreed to some relaxation Treasury
                    control, also Executive <pb facs="0017" n="5" xml:id="pg5"/> Council to be kept
                    fully informed frontier areas policy. First tasks Council to consider strike
                    situation, high cost of living and recent actions of GOB under defence of Burma rules.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Packer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
